    "implementation_guidance": "1. Implement routine screening using validated tool (PHQ-9); establish protocol for positive screens; develop monitoring schedule based on symptom severity; create documentation system for tracking scores over time; implement protocol for suicide risk assessment; establish criteria for psychiatric referral; document screening results and interventions; coordinate with mental health providers; follow up on treatment adherence and response.\n\u2022 Implement validated screening using PHQ-9 for depression (positive \u226510) or GAD-7 for anxiety (positive \u22658).\n\u2022 Apply measurement-based care with symptom score monitoring at each encounter to guide treatment adjustments.\n\u2022 Establish suicide risk assessment protocol using C-SSRS with specific triage pathways based on risk level.\n\u2022 Document first-line medication selection algorithm based on symptom profile and comorbidities.\n\u2022 Implement psychotherapy referral criteria with specific modalities (CBT, IPT, BA) matched to diagnosis.\n\u2022 Apply medication titration schedule with defined dose adjustments at 2-4 week intervals based on response and side effects.\n\u2022 Establish monitoring protocol for treatment response: 50% symptom reduction by week 6, remission by week 12.\n\u2022 Develop individualized care plan with specific goals, interventions, and evaluation metrics using SMART criteria.\n\u2022 Apply risk stratification tool with defined intervention intensity based on risk level (high: weekly contact, moderate: biweekly, low: monthly).\n\u2022 Conduct standardized symptom assessment using validated tools with specific escalation thresholds and intervention pathways.\n\u2022 Apply specific eligibility criteria with defined inclusion and exclusion parameters based on evidence-based guidelines.\n\u2022 Implement risk-stratified screening intervals with specific timing parameters based on previous results and risk factors.\n\u2022 Establish result communication protocol with specific timeframes, documentation requirements, and follow-up pathways based on findings",
