    "id": "asthma_ncm_1",
    "title": "Structured Asthma Self-Management Education Protocol",
    "domain": "Asthma",
    "role": "Nurse Care Manager",
    "implementation_guidance": "1. Assess current asthma knowledge and self-management skills; develop individualized education plan addressing knowledge gaps; provide instruction on proper inhaler technique; create written asthma action plan; teach symptom monitoring and peak flow use; establish protocol for environmental trigger management; document education provided and skills demonstrated; follow up on implementation of self-management behaviors; adjust approach based on control status.\n\u2022 Implement spirometry-based assessment with bronchodilator reversibility testing for diagnosis and monitoring.\n\u2022 Apply validated symptom assessment using ACT (Asthma Control Test, target >19) or CAT (COPD Assessment Test, target <10).\n\u2022 Establish stepwise therapy approach per GINA or GOLD guidelines with specific criteria for step-up/step-down.\n\u2022 Document inhaler technique assessment using standardized checklists with re-education at each visit.\n\u2022 Implement home peak flow monitoring protocol with personal best-based action points (green >80%, yellow 50-80%, red <50%).\n\u2022 Apply environmental trigger assessment and remediation protocol focusing on specific allergens identified by testing.\n\u2022 Establish exacerbation action plan with specific symptom thresholds and medication adjustments.\n\u2022 Develop individualized care plan with specific goals, interventions, and evaluation metrics using SMART criteria.\n\u2022 Apply risk stratification tool with defined intervention intensity based on risk level (high: weekly contact, moderate: biweekly, low: monthly).\n\u2022 Define specific learning objectives with measurable outcomes using Bloom's taxonomy framework.\n\u2022 Implement multimodal teaching methods with specific techniques tailored to learning style assessment results.\n\u2022 Conduct knowledge assessment using standardized tool with pre/post testing and specific mastery thresholds\n\u2022 Implement protocol with specific timeframes: initial assessment within 7 days, follow-up at 30, 60, and 90 days, with comprehensive reassessment at 6 months.\n\u2022 Utilize standardized documentation template with required elements including assessment findings, intervention details, and outcome measures.",
    "expected_outcomes": "Improved asthma control, enhanced self-management behaviors, reduced exacerbations, decreased emergency department visits, better medication adherence, improved quality of life, increased patient confidence in managing asthma.",
    "target_population": "Medicaid-enrolled adults with asthma, particularly those with uncontrolled symptoms or recent exacerbations.",
    "citation": "Gibson PG, Powell H, Coughlan J, et al. Self-management education and regular practitioner review for adults with asthma. Cochrane Database Syst Rev. 2003;(1):CD001117. doi:10.1002/14651858.CD001117",
