    "implementation_guidance": "1. Begin discharge planning early during hospitalization; ensure medication reconciliation and access; schedule follow-up appointment within 7-14 days; provide written discharge instructions with warning signs; establish protocol for post-discharge phone calls within 48-72 hours; document transition plan and interventions; coordinate communication between hospital and outpatient providers; follow up on completion of post-discharge appointments.\n\u2022 Implement standardized discharge risk assessment using LACE index or HOSPITAL score with intervention intensity based on risk level.\n\u2022 Apply medication reconciliation protocol with specific high-risk medication focus (anticoagulants, insulin, opioids, diuretics).\n\u2022 Establish post-discharge contact schedule: phone within 48-72 hours, home visit within 7 days for high-risk patients.\n\u2022 Document teach-back method verification of discharge instructions with minimum 3 key elements confirmed.\n\u2022 Implement red flag symptom identification with specific triage pathways based on condition.\n\u2022 Apply care plan communication to receiving providers within 24 hours of transition using standardized format.\n\u2022 Establish follow-up appointment scheduling pre-discharge with confirmation protocol and transportation assessment.\n\u2022 Conduct comprehensive needs assessment using standardized tool with specific domain scoring and intervention thresholds.\n\u2022 Implement care team communication protocol with defined information exchange requirements, frequency, and modalities.\n\u2022 Apply barrier identification and resolution framework with specific intervention pathways for common barriers (transportation, financial, literacy)\n\u2022 Document baseline and target parameters with specific measurement protocols and documentation requirements.",
