    "implementation_guidance": "1. Review complete medication list; identify potentially nephrotoxic medications; recommend appropriate dose adjustments based on eGFR; evaluate for drug interactions; develop protocol for monitoring medication effects on kidney function; create plan for medication adjustments with disease progression; document medication recommendations and rationale; coordinate with prescribers regarding therapy changes; follow up on implementation of recommendations.\n\u2022 Apply CKD staging based on eGFR and albuminuria categories per KDIGO guidelines.\n\u2022 Implement BP targets of <130/80 mmHg with preferred agents being ACEi or ARB.\n\u2022 Monitor electrolytes and kidney function 1-2 weeks after initiation or dose adjustment of RAS inhibitors.\n\u2022 Apply dietary protein restriction to 0.8 g/kg/day for adults with CKD stages 3-5.\n\u2022 Implement nephrology referral protocol for eGFR <30 mL/min/1.73m\u00b2 or rapid decline (>5 mL/min/1.73m\u00b2/year).\n\u2022 Document medication review with specific focus on nephrotoxic agent avoidance and dose adjustments based on eGFR.\n\u2022 Establish monitoring schedule: eGFR and albuminuria q3-6mo for CKD 3, q1-3mo for CKD 4-5.\n\u2022 Implement therapeutic drug monitoring with specific sampling timing, target ranges, and dose adjustment algorithms.\n\u2022 Apply evidence-based treatment algorithm with specific decision points, intervention selection criteria, and escalation pathways.\n\u2022 Define specific outcome targets with timeframes, measurement parameters, and adjustment thresholds.\n\u2022 Monitor quality metrics with defined process and outcome measures, data collection protocols, and performance thresholds\n\u2022 Utilize standardized documentation template with required elements including assessment findings, intervention details, and outcome measures.\n\u2022 Establish structured follow-up protocol with specific timing, content, and escalation criteria based on patient response.",
    "expected_outcomes": "Reduced medication-related adverse events, appropriate medication dosing, decreased use of nephrotoxic agents, improved medication safety, slowed disease progression, reduced hospitalizations, enhanced medication adherence.",
    "target_population": "Medicaid-enrolled adults with CKD stages 3-5 (non-dialysis), particularly those on multiple medications.",
