    "implementation_guidance": "1. Provide in-home support during early postpartum period; assist with infant feeding and care techniques; offer practical help with household tasks; provide emotional support and active listening; teach infant soothing methods; assist with physical recovery comfort measures; document support activities; coordinate with healthcare providers regarding concerns; provide evidence-based information on postpartum and newborn care; support maternal rest and self-care.\n\u2022 Implement standardized risk assessment using ACOG criteria with specific intervention pathways by risk level.\n\u2022 Apply prenatal visit schedule with content specifications by gestational age.\n\u2022 Establish screening protocol with defined timing for GDM (24-28 weeks), GBS (35-37 weeks), and aneuploidy (NIPT at 10-14 weeks).\n\u2022 Document postpartum follow-up protocol with comprehensive assessment at 2 weeks and 6 weeks.\n\u2022 Implement breastfeeding support protocol with specific assessment using LATCH score and intervention mapping.\n\u2022 Apply perinatal mood disorder screening using Edinburgh scale at intake, 28 weeks, 2 weeks postpartum, and 6 weeks postpartum.\n\u2022 Establish care coordination with defined communication pathways between prenatal, intrapartum, and postpartum providers.\n\u2022 Conduct comprehensive nutritional assessment using validated tools (e.g., SGA, MNA) with anthropometric measurements and laboratory data integration.\n\u2022 Develop individualized meal plan with specific macronutrient distribution, caloric targets, and portion guidance based on nutritional requirements.\n\u2022 Implement dietary monitoring protocol using standardized food records with nutrient analysis and adherence assessment metrics\n\u2022 Document baseline and target parameters with specific measurement protocols and documentation requirements.",
