    "id": "nurse_care_manager_diabetes_paid_1",
    "title": "Problem Areas in Diabetes (PAID) Assessment for Emotional Distress",
    "domain": "Diabetes",
    "role": "Nurse Care Manager",
    "implementation_guidance": "1. Administer the Problem Areas in Diabetes (PAID) scale to assess diabetes-related emotional distress\n2. This 20-item questionnaire helps identify specific areas of diabetes management causing emotional burden\n3. Use results to: identify patients with high distress scores (>40), target specific areas of diabetes management causing the most distress, track changes in emotional distress over time, and guide conversations about emotional aspects of diabetes management.\n\u2022 Utilize point-of-care HbA1c testing with target values of <7.0% for most patients, <8.0% for elderly or those with comorbidities.\n\u2022 Implement SMBG (Self-Monitoring of Blood Glucose) protocol with testing frequency of 1-4 times daily based on medication regimen.\n\u2022 Apply validated risk stratification using UKPDS or ACCORD criteria to determine intervention intensity.\n\u2022 Document baseline and follow-up metrics including HbA1c, lipid panel, microalbumin/creatinine ratio, and estimated GFR.\n\u2022 Establish care plan with specific medication titration parameters based on fasting glucose values (target 80-130 mg/dL).\n\u2022 Implement standardized foot examination using 10g monofilament testing at 5 anatomical sites.\n\u2022 Schedule follow-up intervals based on risk stratification: high-risk q3mo, moderate-risk q6mo, low-risk annually.\n\u2022 Conduct standardized symptom assessment using validated tools with specific escalation thresholds and intervention pathways.\n\u2022 Utilize validated assessment tool with specific scoring parameters, interpretation guidelines, and clinical decision thresholds.\n\u2022 Conduct comprehensive evaluation covering physical, functional, cognitive, and psychosocial domains using standardized instruments.\n\u2022 Follow structured documentation format with required elements including quantitative measures, qualitative observations, and assessment synthesis\n\u2022 Implement protocol with specific timeframes: initial assessment within 7 days, follow-up at 30, 60, and 90 days, with comprehensive reassessment at 6 months.",
    "expected_outcomes": "Improved identification of diabetes-related emotional distress, better targeting of psychological support, reduced depression symptoms, enhanced patient-provider communication about emotional aspects of diabetes, improved quality of life, and better glycemic control through addressing emotional barriers.",
    "target_population": "Medicaid-enrolled individuals with type 2 diabetes, particularly those showing signs of diabetes distress or depression.",
