    "id": "care_coordination_transitions_1",
    "title": "Structured Care Transitions Protocol",
    "domain": "Care Transitions",
    "role": "Dietitian/Nutritionist",
    "implementation_guidance": "1. Implement a structured care transitions protocol that includes: 1) Initiating contact with patients within 48 hours of hospital discharge; 2) Conducting a comprehensive post-discharge assessment using a standardized tool that evaluates medication understanding, follow-up appointment comprehension, warning signs knowledge, and social support needs; 3) Creating a personalized care transitions plan with specific action items and responsible parties; 4) Scheduling follow-up appointments with primary care within 7 days of discharge; 5) Performing medication reconciliation with teach-back verification; and 6) Implementing a graduated follow-up schedule with contacts at 3, 7, 14, and 30 days post-discharge, with intensity adjusted based on risk stratification\n2. The protocol should include clear escalation pathways for clinical concerns and standardized documentation templates to ensure consistent communication across the care team.\n\u2022 Implement standardized discharge risk assessment using LACE index or HOSPITAL score with intervention intensity based on risk level.\n\u2022 Apply medication reconciliation protocol with specific high-risk medication focus (anticoagulants, insulin, opioids, diuretics).\n\u2022 Establish post-discharge contact schedule: phone within 48-72 hours, home visit within 7 days for high-risk patients.\n\u2022 Document teach-back method verification of discharge instructions with minimum 3 key elements confirmed.\n\u2022 Implement red flag symptom identification with specific triage pathways based on condition.\n\u2022 Apply care plan communication to receiving providers within 24 hours of transition using standardized format.\n\u2022 Establish follow-up appointment scheduling pre-discharge with confirmation protocol and transportation assessment.\n\u2022 Conduct comprehensive nutritional assessment using validated tools (e.g., SGA, MNA) with anthropometric measurements and laboratory data integration.\n\u2022 Develop individualized meal plan with specific macronutrient distribution, caloric targets, and portion guidance based on nutritional requirements.\n\u2022 Implement dietary monitoring protocol using standardized food records with nutrient analysis and adherence assessment metrics\n\u2022 Document baseline and target parameters with specific measurement protocols and documentation requirements.",
    "expected_outcomes": "Reduced 30-day hospital readmission rates, improved medication adherence, increased attendance at follow-up appointments, earlier identification of post-discharge complications, and enhanced patient satisfaction with care transitions.",
