    "id": "social_work_cbt_anxiety_1",
    "title": "Structured CBT Protocol for Anxiety",
    "domain": "Anxiety",
    "role": "Dietitian/Nutritionist",
    "implementation_guidance": "1. Implement a structured cognitive-behavioral therapy protocol for anxiety that includes: 1) Conducting a comprehensive assessment using the GAD-7 and specific phobia scales as appropriate; 2) Providing psychoeducation on the cognitive-behavioral model of anxiety using personalized examples from the client's experience; 3) Teaching specific diaphragmatic breathing and progressive muscle relaxation techniques with in-session practice and daily homework assignments; 4) Implementing cognitive restructuring using thought records that identify and challenge specific anxiety-provoking thoughts; 5) Creating a graduated exposure hierarchy with subjective units of distress (SUDS) ratings for each feared situation; and 6) Conducting in-vivo or imaginal exposure exercises with specific pre/post SUDS measurements\n2. The protocol should follow a 12-session structure with clearly defined goals for each session and homework assignments that build progressively.\n\u2022 Implement validated screening using PHQ-9 for depression (positive \u226510) or GAD-7 for anxiety (positive \u22658).\n\u2022 Apply measurement-based care with symptom score monitoring at each encounter to guide treatment adjustments.\n\u2022 Establish suicide risk assessment protocol using C-SSRS with specific triage pathways based on risk level.\n\u2022 Document first-line medication selection algorithm based on symptom profile and comorbidities.\n\u2022 Implement psychotherapy referral criteria with specific modalities (CBT, IPT, BA) matched to diagnosis.\n\u2022 Apply medication titration schedule with defined dose adjustments at 2-4 week intervals based on response and side effects.\n\u2022 Establish monitoring protocol for treatment response: 50% symptom reduction by week 6, remission by week 12.\n\u2022 Conduct comprehensive nutritional assessment using validated tools (e.g., SGA, MNA) with anthropometric measurements and laboratory data integration.\n\u2022 Develop individualized meal plan with specific macronutrient distribution, caloric targets, and portion guidance based on nutritional requirements.\n\u2022 Implement dietary monitoring protocol using standardized food records with nutrient analysis and adherence assessment metrics\n\u2022 Utilize standardized documentation template with required elements including assessment findings, intervention details, and outcome measures.\n\u2022 Establish structured follow-up protocol with specific timing, content, and escalation criteria based on patient response.",
    "expected_outcomes": "Reduced anxiety symptoms as measured by standardized scales, decreased avoidance behaviors, improved daily functioning in previously avoided situations, enhanced self-efficacy in managing anxiety, and development of sustainable coping skills.",
    "target_population": "Adults with generalized anxiety disorder, social anxiety, specific phobias, or panic disorder",
    "citation": "Carpenter JK, Andrews LA, Witcraft SM, Powers MB, Smits JAJ, Hofmann SG. Cognitive behavioral therapy for anxiety and related disorders: A meta-analysis of randomized placebo-controlled trials. Depress Anxiety. 2018;35(6):502-514. doi:10.1002/da.22728",
    "evidence_level": "A - Strong",
