    "id": "pharmacy_tech_med_sync_1",
    "title": "Medication Synchronization Program Implementation",
    "domain": "Medication Adherence",
    "role": "Pharmacy Technician",
    "implementation_guidance": "1. Implement a structured medication synchronization program where pharmacy technicians coordinate the refill schedule for all of a patient's chronic medications to be filled on the same day each month\n2. The program should include: 1) Identifying eligible patients through prescription refill data analysis; 2) Conducting initial patient outreach to explain the program benefits; 3) Performing a comprehensive medication inventory and reconciliation; 4) Calculating appropriate short fills to align medication schedules; 5) Setting up a consistent monthly pickup or delivery date; and 6) Establishing a proactive monthly contact protocol to address any medication changes or issues before the scheduled fill date\n3. Pharmacy technicians should document all patient interactions and maintain a dedicated calendar system for tracking synchronized patients.\n\u2022 Implement validated adherence assessment using MMAS-8 (positive <6) or BMQ (Beliefs about Medicines Questionnaire).\n\u2022 Apply adherence barrier identification using standardized questionnaire with specific intervention mapping.\n\u2022 Establish medication regimen simplification protocol with specific consolidation strategies (once-daily dosing, fixed-dose combinations).\n\u2022 Document adherence monitoring using PDC (Proportion of Days Covered) calculation with target >80%.\n\u2022 Implement reminder system selection algorithm based on patient preferences and technological access.\n\u2022 Apply motivational interviewing technique with specific focus on necessity beliefs and concern mitigation.\n\u2022 Establish follow-up protocol with adherence reassessment at 30, 60, and 90 days post-intervention.\n\u2022 Collect comprehensive medication history using standardized interview tool with specific verification process using multiple sources.\n\u2022 Implement refill management protocol with specific timing parameters, authorization requirements, and synchronization procedures.\n\u2022 Apply inventory management procedures with par level monitoring, expiration tracking, and specific documentation requirements",
    "expected_outcomes": "Improved medication adherence rates, reduced gaps in therapy, increased patient satisfaction with pharmacy services, decreased pharmacy workflow bottlenecks, and improved chronic disease management outcomes.",
    "target_population": "Patients taking multiple chronic medications, particularly older adults and those with complex medication regimens",
    "citation": "Kadia NK, Schroeder MN. Community Pharmacy-Based Adherence Programs and the Role of Pharmacy Technicians: A Review. J Pharm Technol. 2015;31(2):51-57. doi:10.1177/8755122515572809",
