    "implementation_guidance": "1. Implement a comprehensive medication therapy management protocol for patients with diabetes that includes: 1) Systematic review of all medications including prescription, over-the-counter, and supplements; 2) Assessment of medication appropriateness using current guidelines; 3) Evaluation of medication adherence using standardized tools; 4) Identification of drug therapy problems including inappropriate dosing, drug interactions, and adverse effects; 5) Development of a personalized care plan with specific medication-related goals; and 6) Regular follow-up at 2-4 week intervals until glycemic targets are achieved, then every 3 months\n2. Document all interventions and clinical outcomes including changes in HbA1c, blood pressure, lipids, and achievement of individualized goals.\n\u2022 Utilize point-of-care HbA1c testing with target values of <7.0% for most patients, <8.0% for elderly or those with comorbidities.\n\u2022 Implement SMBG (Self-Monitoring of Blood Glucose) protocol with testing frequency of 1-4 times daily based on medication regimen.\n\u2022 Apply validated risk stratification using UKPDS or ACCORD criteria to determine intervention intensity.\n\u2022 Document baseline and follow-up metrics including HbA1c, lipid panel, microalbumin/creatinine ratio, and estimated GFR.\n\u2022 Establish care plan with specific medication titration parameters based on fasting glucose values (target 80-130 mg/dL).\n\u2022 Implement standardized foot examination using 10g monofilament testing at 5 anatomical sites.\n\u2022 Schedule follow-up intervals based on risk stratification: high-risk q3mo, moderate-risk q6mo, low-risk annually.\n\u2022 Conduct comprehensive medication review using standardized assessment tool with focus on appropriateness, effectiveness, safety, and adherence domains.\n\u2022 Implement therapeutic drug monitoring with specific sampling timing, target ranges, and dose adjustment algorithms.\n\u2022 Apply evidence-based treatment algorithm with specific decision points, intervention selection criteria, and escalation pathways.\n\u2022 Define specific outcome targets with timeframes, measurement parameters, and adjustment thresholds.\n\u2022 Monitor quality metrics with defined process and outcome measures, data collection protocols, and performance thresholds\n\u2022 Utilize standardized documentation template with required elements including assessment findings, intervention details, and outcome measures.",
    "expected_outcomes": "Improved glycemic control with reduction in HbA1c, optimization of medication regimens, decreased medication-related adverse events, enhanced medication adherence, and improved patient understanding of diabetes medications.",
