    "domain": "Postnatal",
    "role": "Dietitian/Nutritionist",
    "implementation_guidance": "1. Conduct a structured comprehensive biopsychosocial assessment for all postpartum patients that includes: 1) Screen for postpartum depression using a validated tool (e.g., Edinburgh Postnatal Depression Scale) at 2 weeks, 6 weeks, and 3 months postpartum, 2) Assess for intimate partner violence using a standardized screening tool, 3) Evaluate chronic disease management needs, particularly for conditions affected by pregnancy (e.g., hypertension, diabetes), 4) Screen for social determinants of health using a standardized tool covering housing, food security, and transportation, 5) Document all findings in the patient record with specific action plans for identified issues, 6) Implement a referral protocol for positive screens with warm handoffs to appropriate services, and 7) Schedule follow-up assessments based on identified risks.\n\u2022 Implement standardized risk assessment using ACOG criteria with specific intervention pathways by risk level.\n\u2022 Apply prenatal visit schedule with content specifications by gestational age.\n\u2022 Establish screening protocol with defined timing for GDM (24-28 weeks), GBS (35-37 weeks), and aneuploidy (NIPT at 10-14 weeks).\n\u2022 Document postpartum follow-up protocol with comprehensive assessment at 2 weeks and 6 weeks.\n\u2022 Implement breastfeeding support protocol with specific assessment using LATCH score and intervention mapping.\n\u2022 Apply perinatal mood disorder screening using Edinburgh scale at intake, 28 weeks, 2 weeks postpartum, and 6 weeks postpartum.\n\u2022 Establish care coordination with defined communication pathways between prenatal, intrapartum, and postpartum providers.\n\u2022 Conduct comprehensive nutritional assessment using validated tools (e.g., SGA, MNA) with anthropometric measurements and laboratory data integration.\n\u2022 Develop individualized meal plan with specific macronutrient distribution, caloric targets, and portion guidance based on nutritional requirements.\n\u2022 Implement dietary monitoring protocol using standardized food records with nutrient analysis and adherence assessment metrics.\n\u2022 Utilize validated assessment tool with specific scoring parameters, interpretation guidelines, and clinical decision thresholds.\n\u2022 Conduct comprehensive evaluation covering physical, functional, cognitive, and psychosocial domains using standardized instruments.\n\u2022 Follow structured documentation format with required elements including quantitative measures, qualitative observations, and assessment synthesis\n\u2022 Document baseline and target parameters with specific measurement protocols and documentation requirements.",
    "expected_outcomes": "Earlier identification and intervention for mental health concerns, improved management of chronic conditions, increased connection to social services, reduced postpartum complications, and enhanced maternal wellbeing and functioning.",
    "target_population": "All postpartum individuals, with particular attention to those with pre-existing mental health conditions, pregnancy complications, or identified social risk factors.",
