    "implementation_guidance": "1. Establish a structured care coordination program for postpartum patients that includes: 1) Create a comprehensive postpartum care plan before hospital discharge that addresses both short and long-term health needs, 2) Schedule a clear sequence of follow-up appointments with appropriate providers based on risk factors and pregnancy complications, 3) Implement a warm handoff protocol for transition to primary care with direct communication between providers, 4) Ensure all pregnancy complications and outcomes are documented in a standardized format accessible to future providers, 5) Provide patients with a portable health record summarizing pregnancy outcomes and follow-up needs, 6) Conduct follow-up calls at 1 week and 1 month after transition to confirm successful connection to ongoing care, and 7) Address barriers to care continuity as they arise.\n\u2022 Implement standardized risk assessment using ACOG criteria with specific intervention pathways by risk level.\n\u2022 Apply prenatal visit schedule with content specifications by gestational age.\n\u2022 Establish screening protocol with defined timing for GDM (24-28 weeks), GBS (35-37 weeks), and aneuploidy (NIPT at 10-14 weeks).\n\u2022 Document postpartum follow-up protocol with comprehensive assessment at 2 weeks and 6 weeks.\n\u2022 Implement breastfeeding support protocol with specific assessment using LATCH score and intervention mapping.\n\u2022 Apply perinatal mood disorder screening using Edinburgh scale at intake, 28 weeks, 2 weeks postpartum, and 6 weeks postpartum.\n\u2022 Establish care coordination with defined communication pathways between prenatal, intrapartum, and postpartum providers.\n\u2022 Conduct comprehensive needs assessment using standardized tool with specific domain scoring and intervention thresholds.\n\u2022 Implement care team communication protocol with defined information exchange requirements, frequency, and modalities.\n\u2022 Apply barrier identification and resolution framework with specific intervention pathways for common barriers (transportation, financial, literacy)\n\u2022 Document baseline and target parameters with specific measurement protocols and documentation requirements.",
