    "implementation_guidance": "1. Implement a comprehensive approach to hypertension management that includes: 1) Conduct regular screenings and assessments; 2) Develop individualized care plans; 3) Provide patient education using teach-back methods; 4) Coordinate care with specialists; 5) Monitor outcomes and adjust interventions as needed; 6) Address social determinants of health; 7) Utilize evidence-based protocols; 8) Engage family and caregivers in the care process; 9) Document interventions and outcomes; 10) Follow up regularly to ensure adherence and address barriers.\n\u2022 Implement standardized BP measurement protocol using validated devices with appropriate cuff size (width 40% of arm circumference).\n\u2022 Target BP values: <130/80 mmHg for most patients, <140/90 mmHg for elderly (>65 years).\n\u2022 Utilize DASH dietary approach with sodium restriction to <2,300 mg/day.\n\u2022 Apply medication titration algorithm based on renin-angiotensin system blockade as first-line therapy.\n\u2022 Implement home BP monitoring protocol with minimum 14 readings/week (morning and evening).\n\u2022 Document medication adherence using validated PDC (Proportion of Days Covered) metric with target >80%.\n\u2022 Schedule follow-up intervals based on BP control: uncontrolled q2-4wk, controlled q3-6mo.\n\u2022 Conduct medication therapy management using standardized framework with specific problem identification, care plan development, and follow-up protocols.\n\u2022 Perform medication reconciliation using standardized process with specific discrepancy resolution pathways and documentation requirements.\n\u2022 Apply evidence-based treatment algorithm with specific decision points, intervention selection criteria, and escalation pathways.\n\u2022 Define specific outcome targets with timeframes, measurement parameters, and adjustment thresholds.\n\u2022 Monitor quality metrics with defined process and outcome measures, data collection protocols, and performance thresholds\n\u2022 Implement protocol with specific timeframes: initial assessment within 7 days, follow-up at 30, 60, and 90 days, with comprehensive reassessment at 6 months.",
