    "id": "depression_primary_care_provider_1",
    "title": "Evidence-Based Depression Management for Primary Care Providers",
    "domain": "Depression",
    "role": "Clinical Pharmacist",
    "implementation_guidance": "1. Implement a comprehensive approach to depression management that includes: 1) Conduct regular screenings and assessments; 2) Develop individualized care plans; 3) Provide patient education using teach-back methods; 4) Coordinate care with specialists; 5) Monitor outcomes and adjust interventions as needed; 6) Address social determinants of health; 7) Utilize evidence-based protocols; 8) Engage family and caregivers in the care process; 9) Document interventions and outcomes; 10) Follow up regularly to ensure adherence and address barriers.\n\u2022 Implement validated screening using PHQ-9 for depression (positive \u226510) or GAD-7 for anxiety (positive \u22658).\n\u2022 Apply measurement-based care with symptom score monitoring at each encounter to guide treatment adjustments.\n\u2022 Establish suicide risk assessment protocol using C-SSRS with specific triage pathways based on risk level.\n\u2022 Document first-line medication selection algorithm based on symptom profile and comorbidities.\n\u2022 Implement psychotherapy referral criteria with specific modalities (CBT, IPT, BA) matched to diagnosis.\n\u2022 Apply medication titration schedule with defined dose adjustments at 2-4 week intervals based on response and side effects.\n\u2022 Establish monitoring protocol for treatment response: 50% symptom reduction by week 6, remission by week 12.\n\u2022 Conduct comprehensive medication review using standardized assessment tool with focus on appropriateness, effectiveness, safety, and adherence domains.\n\u2022 Perform drug interaction screening using validated software with specific severity rating system and intervention protocol.\n\u2022 Implement therapeutic drug monitoring with specific sampling timing, target ranges, and dose adjustment algorithms.\n\u2022 Apply evidence-based treatment algorithm with specific decision points, intervention selection criteria, and escalation pathways.\n\u2022 Define specific outcome targets with timeframes, measurement parameters, and adjustment thresholds.\n\u2022 Monitor quality metrics with defined process and outcome measures, data collection protocols, and performance thresholds\n\u2022 Utilize standardized documentation template with required elements including assessment findings, intervention details, and outcome measures.\n\u2022 Establish structured follow-up protocol with specific timing, content, and escalation criteria based on patient response.",
    "expected_outcomes": "Improved depression management, reduced complications, enhanced quality of life, decreased emergency department visits and hospitalizations, improved patient satisfaction, better medication adherence, increased patient self-management skills, reduced healthcare disparities.",
    "target_population": "Medicaid-enrolled individuals, particularly those from underserved communities, racial and ethnic minorities, and those facing barriers to healthcare access.",
    "citation": "Agency for Healthcare Research and Quality. Evidence-Based Practice Guidelines for Depression Management in Primary Care Settings. https://www.ahrq.gov/research/findings/evidence-based-reports/search.html. Published 2023. Accessed May 29, 2025.",
