    "implementation_guidance": "1. Implement a comprehensive approach to asthma management that includes: 1) Conduct regular screenings and assessments; 2) Develop individualized care plans; 3) Provide patient education using teach-back methods; 4) Coordinate care with specialists; 5) Monitor outcomes and adjust interventions as needed; 6) Address social determinants of health; 7) Utilize evidence-based protocols; 8) Engage family and caregivers in the care process; 9) Document interventions and outcomes; 10) Follow up regularly to ensure adherence and address barriers.\n\u2022 Implement spirometry-based assessment with bronchodilator reversibility testing for diagnosis and monitoring.\n\u2022 Apply validated symptom assessment using ACT (Asthma Control Test, target >19) or CAT (COPD Assessment Test, target <10).\n\u2022 Establish stepwise therapy approach per GINA or GOLD guidelines with specific criteria for step-up/step-down.\n\u2022 Document inhaler technique assessment using standardized checklists with re-education at each visit.\n\u2022 Implement home peak flow monitoring protocol with personal best-based action points (green >80%, yellow 50-80%, red <50%).\n\u2022 Apply environmental trigger assessment and remediation protocol focusing on specific allergens identified by testing.\n\u2022 Establish exacerbation action plan with specific symptom thresholds and medication adjustments.\n\u2022 Apply risk stratification tool with defined intervention intensity based on risk level (high: weekly contact, moderate: biweekly, low: monthly).\n\u2022 Apply evidence-based treatment algorithm with specific decision points, intervention selection criteria, and escalation pathways.\n\u2022 Define specific outcome targets with timeframes, measurement parameters, and adjustment thresholds.\n\u2022 Monitor quality metrics with defined process and outcome measures, data collection protocols, and performance thresholds\n\u2022 Implement protocol with specific timeframes: initial assessment within 7 days, follow-up at 30, 60, and 90 days, with comprehensive reassessment at 6 months.\n\u2022 Utilize standardized documentation template with required elements including assessment findings, intervention details, and outcome measures.",
