    "implementation_guidance": "1. Implement a comprehensive approach to heart failure management that includes: 1) Conduct regular screenings and assessments; 2) Develop individualized care plans; 3) Provide patient education using teach-back methods; 4) Coordinate care with specialists; 5) Monitor outcomes and adjust interventions as needed; 6) Address social determinants of health; 7) Utilize evidence-based protocols; 8) Engage family and caregivers in the care process; 9) Document interventions and outcomes; 10) Follow up regularly to ensure adherence and address barriers.\n\u2022 Implement NYHA functional classification assessment at each encounter to guide therapy intensity.\n\u2022 Monitor daily weights with alert parameters for gains >2 lbs/day or >5 lbs/week.\n\u2022 Titrate GDMT (Guideline-Directed Medical Therapy) according to specific dose escalation protocols for ARNI/ACEi/ARB, beta-blockers, MRAs, and SGLT2i.\n\u2022 Apply validated risk stratification using MAGGIC or EMPHASIS-HF risk scores.\n\u2022 Implement fluid restriction protocol (1.5-2L/day) for patients with hyponatremia or refractory fluid retention.\n\u2022 Document medication reconciliation with specific focus on NSAID avoidance and diuretic adjustment parameters.\n\u2022 Establish action plan with specific symptom-based decision points for self-management vs\n2. clinical contact.\n\u2022 Conduct comprehensive medication review using standardized assessment tool with focus on appropriateness, effectiveness, safety, and adherence domains.\n\u2022 Perform drug interaction screening using validated software with specific severity rating system and intervention protocol.\n\u2022 Implement therapeutic drug monitoring with specific sampling timing, target ranges, and dose adjustment algorithms.\n\u2022 Apply evidence-based treatment algorithm with specific decision points, intervention selection criteria, and escalation pathways.\n\u2022 Define specific outcome targets with timeframes, measurement parameters, and adjustment thresholds.\n\u2022 Monitor quality metrics with defined process and outcome measures, data collection protocols, and performance thresholds\n\u2022 Implement protocol with specific timeframes: initial assessment within 7 days, follow-up at 30, 60, and 90 days, with comprehensive reassessment at 6 months.\n\u2022 Document baseline and target parameters with specific measurement protocols and documentation requirements.",
