    "role": "Clinical Pharmacist",
    "implementation_guidance": "1. Implement a comprehensive approach to post mi management that includes: 1) Conduct regular screenings and assessments; 2) Develop individualized care plans; 3) Provide patient education using teach-back methods; 4) Coordinate care with specialists; 5) Monitor outcomes and adjust interventions as needed; 6) Address social determinants of health; 7) Utilize evidence-based protocols; 8) Engage family and caregivers in the care process; 9) Document interventions and outcomes; 10) Follow up regularly to ensure adherence and address barriers.\n\u2022 Implement cardiac rehabilitation referral protocol with enrollment target within 7-10 days post-discharge.\n\u2022 Apply medication optimization algorithm for GDMT (ACEi/ARB, beta-blocker, statin, antiplatelet) with specific agent and dose targets.\n\u2022 Establish symptom monitoring protocol using NYHA classification with specific action thresholds.\n\u2022 Document risk factor modification targets: BP <130/80 mmHg, LDL <70 mg/dL, HbA1c <7%, smoking cessation.\n\u2022 Implement activity progression protocol with MET-based exercise prescription and weekly advancement schedule.\n\u2022 Apply psychosocial assessment for post-MI depression and anxiety using PHQ-9 and GAD-7 with referral thresholds.\n\u2022 Establish follow-up schedule: cardiology within 2 weeks, primary care within 4 weeks, and cardiac rehab 3x weekly for 12 weeks.\n\u2022 Conduct comprehensive medication review using standardized assessment tool with focus on appropriateness, effectiveness, safety, and adherence domains.\n\u2022 Perform drug interaction screening using validated software with specific severity rating system and intervention protocol.\n\u2022 Implement therapeutic drug monitoring with specific sampling timing, target ranges, and dose adjustment algorithms.\n\u2022 Apply evidence-based treatment algorithm with specific decision points, intervention selection criteria, and escalation pathways.\n\u2022 Define specific outcome targets with timeframes, measurement parameters, and adjustment thresholds.\n\u2022 Monitor quality metrics with defined process and outcome measures, data collection protocols, and performance thresholds\n\u2022 Utilize standardized documentation template with required elements including assessment findings, intervention details, and outcome measures.",
    "expected_outcomes": "Improved post mi management, reduced complications, enhanced quality of life, decreased emergency department visits and hospitalizations, improved patient satisfaction, better medication adherence, increased patient self-management skills, reduced healthcare disparities.",
