    "implementation_guidance": "1. Implement a targeted approach to depression management that includes: 1) Conduct comprehensive assessments; 2) Develop personalized care plans; 3) Provide culturally appropriate education; 4) Coordinate with specialists; 5) Monitor outcomes regularly; 6) Address social determinants of health; 7) Follow evidence-based protocols; 8) Engage patients and families; 9) Document interventions and outcomes; 10) Follow up to ensure adherence and address barriers.\n\u2022 Implement validated screening using PHQ-9 for depression (positive \u226510) or GAD-7 for anxiety (positive \u22658).\n\u2022 Apply measurement-based care with symptom score monitoring at each encounter to guide treatment adjustments.\n\u2022 Establish suicide risk assessment protocol using C-SSRS with specific triage pathways based on risk level.\n\u2022 Document first-line medication selection algorithm based on symptom profile and comorbidities.\n\u2022 Implement psychotherapy referral criteria with specific modalities (CBT, IPT, BA) matched to diagnosis.\n\u2022 Apply medication titration schedule with defined dose adjustments at 2-4 week intervals based on response and side effects.\n\u2022 Establish monitoring protocol for treatment response: 50% symptom reduction by week 6, remission by week 12.\n\u2022 Facilitate birth plan development using standardized template with specific preference documentation for labor, delivery, and postpartum phases.\n\u2022 Implement continuous labor support with specific comfort measure techniques, positioning protocols, and progress assessment parameters.\n\u2022 Provide structured postpartum support with specific assessment for feeding, emotional wellbeing, and recovery milestones.\n\u2022 Apply evidence-based treatment algorithm with specific decision points, intervention selection criteria, and escalation pathways.\n\u2022 Define specific outcome targets with timeframes, measurement parameters, and adjustment thresholds.\n\u2022 Monitor quality metrics with defined process and outcome measures, data collection protocols, and performance thresholds\n\u2022 Establish structured follow-up protocol with specific timing, content, and escalation criteria based on patient response.",
    "expected_outcomes": "Improved depression outcomes, reduced complications, enhanced quality of life, decreased healthcare utilization, improved patient satisfaction, better treatment adherence, increased self-management skills, reduced healthcare disparities.",
    "target_population": "Medicaid-enrolled individuals from underserved communities, particularly those facing barriers to healthcare access.",
    "citation": "Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services. Evidence-Based Depression Management Guidelines for Medicaid Populations. https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid/quality-of-care/quality-improvement-initiatives/. Published 2023. Accessed May 29, 2025.",
