    "implementation_guidance": "1. Develop and implement a structured care coordination system for patients with asthma that connects schools, homes, and community resources\n2. Create protocols for coordinating multidisciplinary care teams, establish systems for tracking asthma action plan implementation, implement follow-up procedures after exacerbations, and facilitate communication between healthcare providers, schools, and families\n3. Establish documentation standards and implement metrics to evaluate care coordination effectiveness\n4. Focus on ensuring comprehensive management by addressing environmental triggers, providing education, and facilitating access to care.\n\u2022 Implement spirometry-based assessment with bronchodilator reversibility testing for diagnosis and monitoring.\n\u2022 Apply validated symptom assessment using ACT (Asthma Control Test, target >19) or CAT (COPD Assessment Test, target <10).\n\u2022 Establish stepwise therapy approach per GINA or GOLD guidelines with specific criteria for step-up/step-down.\n\u2022 Document inhaler technique assessment using standardized checklists with re-education at each visit.\n\u2022 Implement home peak flow monitoring protocol with personal best-based action points (green >80%, yellow 50-80%, red <50%).\n\u2022 Apply environmental trigger assessment and remediation protocol focusing on specific allergens identified by testing.\n\u2022 Establish exacerbation action plan with specific symptom thresholds and medication adjustments.\n\u2022 Conduct comprehensive needs assessment using standardized tool with specific domain scoring and intervention thresholds.\n\u2022 Implement care team communication protocol with defined information exchange requirements, frequency, and modalities.\n\u2022 Apply barrier identification and resolution framework with specific intervention pathways for common barriers (transportation, financial, literacy).\n\u2022 Apply evidence-based treatment algorithm with specific decision points, intervention selection criteria, and escalation pathways.\n\u2022 Define specific outcome targets with timeframes, measurement parameters, and adjustment thresholds.\n\u2022 Monitor quality metrics with defined process and outcome measures, data collection protocols, and performance thresholds\n\u2022 Implement protocol with specific timeframes: initial assessment within 7 days, follow-up at 30, 60, and 90 days, with comprehensive reassessment at 6 months.",
    "expected_outcomes": "Improved care coordination, reduced care fragmentation, decreased emergency department visits and hospitalizations, enhanced patient and family engagement, improved asthma control, and better quality of life for patients with asthma.",
    "target_population": "Patients with asthma, particularly children and those with complex care needs or frequent exacerbations.",
    "citation": "Global Initiative for Asthma. Global Strategy for Asthma Management and Prevention, 2023. Available from: www.ginasthma.org",
