    "role": "Clinical Pharmacist",
    "implementation_guidance": "1. Implement pharmacist-led medication management services for heart failure patients\n2. Conduct comprehensive medication reconciliation at care transitions to prevent medication errors\n3. Identify and resolve drug-related problems through systematic medication reviews\n4. Optimize guideline-directed medical therapy through collaborative practice agreements with physicians\n5. Provide detailed patient counseling on medication use and adherence strategies\n6. Monitor for drug interactions and adverse effects with regular follow-up\n7. Titrate medications in collaboration with the care team following established protocols\n8. Educate patients on medication rationale, dosing, and side effects to improve understanding and adherence\n9. Develop standardized documentation templates to track interventions and outcomes.\n\u2022 Implement NYHA functional classification assessment at each encounter to guide therapy intensity.\n\u2022 Monitor daily weights with alert parameters for gains >2 lbs/day or >5 lbs/week.\n\u2022 Titrate GDMT (Guideline-Directed Medical Therapy) according to specific dose escalation protocols for ARNI/ACEi/ARB, beta-blockers, MRAs, and SGLT2i.\n\u2022 Apply validated risk stratification using MAGGIC or EMPHASIS-HF risk scores.\n\u2022 Implement fluid restriction protocol (1.5-2L/day) for patients with hyponatremia or refractory fluid retention.\n\u2022 Document medication reconciliation with specific focus on NSAID avoidance and diuretic adjustment parameters.\n\u2022 Establish action plan with specific symptom-based decision points for self-management vs\n10. clinical contact.\n\u2022 Implement therapeutic drug monitoring with specific sampling timing, target ranges, and dose adjustment algorithms.\n\u2022 Apply evidence-based treatment algorithm with specific decision points, intervention selection criteria, and escalation pathways.\n\u2022 Define specific outcome targets with timeframes, measurement parameters, and adjustment thresholds.\n\u2022 Monitor quality metrics with defined process and outcome measures, data collection protocols, and performance thresholds\n\u2022 Implement protocol with specific timeframes: initial assessment within 7 days, follow-up at 30, 60, and 90 days, with comprehensive reassessment at 6 months.\n\u2022 Document baseline and target parameters with specific measurement protocols and documentation requirements.",
    "expected_outcomes": "Reduced medication errors and adverse drug events, improved guideline-directed medical therapy adherence and optimization, decreased 30-day readmissions, enhanced patient understanding of medications, and improved clinical outcomes through optimal pharmacotherapy.",
    "target_population": "Patients with heart failure across the spectrum of disease severity, with particular focus on those with complex medication regimens, polypharmacy, recent care transitions, or difficulty achieving optimal medical therapy.",
    "citation": "Milfred-LaForest SK, Chow SL, DiDomenico RJ, et al. Clinical Pharmacy Services in Heart Failure: An Opinion Paper from the Heart Failure Society of America and American College of Clinical Pharmacy Cardiology Practice and Research Network. Journal of Cardiac Failure. 2013;19(5):354-69.",
    "evidence_level": "A - Strong",
