    "implementation_guidance": "1. Develop and implement a structured protocol for care coordinators to track patient progress in anxiety management\n2. Create systems for tracking patient progress using standardized assessment tools like GAD-7 at regular intervals\n3. Implement strategies to promote patient engagement including reminder systems, motivational interviewing techniques, and addressing barriers to participation\n4. Establish processes for facilitating stepped adjustments in care based on symptom severity and treatment response\n5. Create protocols for regular check-ins with patients via phone, text, or patient portal based on patient preference and risk level\n6. Develop documentation standards to ensure consistent tracking of interventions and outcomes\n7. Implement metrics to evaluate care coordination effectiveness including symptom improvement, treatment adherence, and patient satisfaction.\n\u2022 Implement validated screening using PHQ-9 for depression (positive \u226510) or GAD-7 for anxiety (positive \u22658).\n\u2022 Apply measurement-based care with symptom score monitoring at each encounter to guide treatment adjustments.\n\u2022 Establish suicide risk assessment protocol using C-SSRS with specific triage pathways based on risk level.\n\u2022 Document first-line medication selection algorithm based on symptom profile and comorbidities.\n\u2022 Implement psychotherapy referral criteria with specific modalities (CBT, IPT, BA) matched to diagnosis.\n\u2022 Apply medication titration schedule with defined dose adjustments at 2-4 week intervals based on response and side effects.\n\u2022 Establish monitoring protocol for treatment response: 50% symptom reduction by week 6, remission by week 12.\n\u2022 Conduct comprehensive needs assessment using standardized tool with specific domain scoring and intervention thresholds.\n\u2022 Implement care team communication protocol with defined information exchange requirements, frequency, and modalities.\n\u2022 Apply barrier identification and resolution framework with specific intervention pathways for common barriers (transportation, financial, literacy)\n\u2022 Establish structured follow-up protocol with specific timing, content, and escalation criteria based on patient response.",
    "expected_outcomes": "Improved treatment adherence, enhanced symptom monitoring, earlier identification of treatment non-response, better care continuity, increased patient engagement in anxiety management, and improved clinical outcomes.",
    "target_population": "Patients with diagnosed anxiety disorders across the spectrum of severity, with particular focus on those at risk for treatment non-adherence, those with comorbid conditions, or those transitioning between levels of care.",
    "citation": "Stein MB, Sareen J. Generalized Anxiety Disorder. The New England Journal of Medicine. 2015;373(21):2059-68.",
