    "implementation_guidance": "1. Develop and implement a structured protocol for care coordinators to address food insecurity\n2. Create systems for routine food insecurity screening using the validated two-item Hunger Vital Sign tool, integrated into standard clinical workflows\n3. Implement resource connection processes including referrals to federal nutrition assistance programs (SNAP, WIC, TEFAP), local food pantries, meal delivery services, and produce prescription programs\n4. Establish follow-up procedures to confirm successful connection to resources and reassess food security status at defined intervals\n5. Create documentation standards in the electronic health record with structured data elements for screening results, referrals made, and outcomes\n6. Implement team-based approaches to addressing food needs with clear role delineation among clinical and non-clinical staff\n7. Develop metrics to evaluate care coordination effectiveness including screening rates, successful resource connections, and improvements in food security status.\n\u2022 Implement validated nutritional assessment using MNA (Mini Nutritional Assessment) or SGA (Subjective Global Assessment).\n\u2022 Apply anthropometric measurements including BMI, waist circumference, and body composition analysis.\n\u2022 Establish caloric needs calculation using Mifflin-St Jeor equation with activity factor adjustments.\n\u2022 Document macronutrient distribution targets: 45-65% carbohydrates, 10-35% protein, 20-35% fat.\n\u2022 Implement meal planning using plate method (\u00bd vegetables, \u00bc protein, \u00bc carbohydrates) or carbohydrate counting.\n\u2022 Apply food security assessment using USDA 2-item screener with specific resource connection pathways.\n\u2022 Establish monitoring protocol with defined metrics (weight, labs, symptom scores) and reassessment intervals.\n\u2022 Implement dietary monitoring protocol using standardized food records with nutrient analysis and adherence assessment metrics.\n\u2022 Apply evidence-based treatment algorithm with specific decision points, intervention selection criteria, and escalation pathways.\n\u2022 Define specific outcome targets with timeframes, measurement parameters, and adjustment thresholds.\n\u2022 Monitor quality metrics with defined process and outcome measures, data collection protocols, and performance thresholds\n\u2022 Implement protocol with specific timeframes: initial assessment within 7 days, follow-up at 30, 60, and 90 days, with comprehensive reassessment at 6 months.",
