    "implementation_guidance": "1. Implement systematic screening and risk stratification for CKD in high-risk populations\n2. Develop protocols for routine screening in patients with diabetes or hypertension, implement eGFR and albuminuria testing systems, create risk stratification algorithms based on test results, establish monitoring intervals based on CKD stage, develop individualized follow-up protocols, and implement metrics to track screening effectiveness.\n\u2022 Apply CKD staging based on eGFR and albuminuria categories per KDIGO guidelines.\n\u2022 Implement BP targets of <130/80 mmHg with preferred agents being ACEi or ARB.\n\u2022 Monitor electrolytes and kidney function 1-2 weeks after initiation or dose adjustment of RAS inhibitors.\n\u2022 Apply dietary protein restriction to 0.8 g/kg/day for adults with CKD stages 3-5.\n\u2022 Implement nephrology referral protocol for eGFR <30 mL/min/1.73m\u00b2 or rapid decline (>5 mL/min/1.73m\u00b2/year).\n\u2022 Document medication review with specific focus on nephrotoxic agent avoidance and dose adjustments based on eGFR.\n\u2022 Establish monitoring schedule: eGFR and albuminuria q3-6mo for CKD 3, q1-3mo for CKD 4-5.\n\u2022 Perform drug interaction screening using validated software with specific severity rating system and intervention protocol.\n\u2022 Implement therapeutic drug monitoring with specific sampling timing, target ranges, and dose adjustment algorithms.\n\u2022 Apply specific eligibility criteria with defined inclusion and exclusion parameters based on evidence-based guidelines.\n\u2022 Implement risk-stratified screening intervals with specific timing parameters based on previous results and risk factors.\n\u2022 Establish result communication protocol with specific timeframes, documentation requirements, and follow-up pathways based on findings",
